  "question": {
    "text": "If the function $f(x)=\\frac{\\tan (\\tan x)-\\sin (\\sin x)}{\\tan x-\\sin x}$ is continuous at $\\mathrm{x}=0$, then $f(0)$ is equal to ________",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{\\frac{\\tan (\\tan x)-\\tan x}{\\tan ^3 x} \\frac{\\tan ^3 x}{x^3}+\\frac{\\tan x-\\sin x}{x^3}+\\frac{\\sin x-\\sin (\\sin x)}{\\sin ^3 x} \\frac{\\sin ^3 x}{x^3}}{\\frac{\\tan x-\\sin x}{x^3}}$<br/>$=\\frac{\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{6}}{\\frac{1}{2}}=2$",
    "image": null
  },
